📗
  🛤 A registered route: a method, a pattern and the handler for the requests
  that match them. The pattern is taken apart once, when the route is made,
  into segments of six kinds. They are numbered in the order in which one is
  preferred to another when two routes match the same path:

    0  todos       that text
    1  :id:int     one segment that is an integer
    2  :id:int?    the same, or the end of the path
    3  :name       any one segment
    4  :name?      any one segment, or the end of the path
    5  *rest       whatever is left, which may be nothing

  Registering a route gives it back, and it takes notes: text under a name,
  for middleware to act on. A request knows the route it matched (🛤 r❗️ is
  its pattern, 🏷🔸🛤 r key❗️ one of its notes) before any middleware runs.

