  📗
    Has the route stand aside for the others, and returns it. This is for a
    catch-all that answers whatever nothing else did, such as a directory of
    files at the root of a site, or a page to fall back on.

    Such a route answers its own method on a path that no other route has,
    and nothing else. To any other method it is not there: when no route has
    a request's method, the answer is a 405 that lists the methods of the
    routes that match the path, and a route that stands aside is not counted
    among them. Without that it would make a 405 of every path that has no
    route, for every method but its own, where a client should be told 404.
    And a path that another route has, for whatever method, is that route's:
    a GET for a path the app only takes a POST on is a 405 that says so, and
    not the page or a file that is not there.
